WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.944
Taikang, grandson of Yu the Great, inherited the throne of Xia.

00:00:05.294 --> 00:00:09.278
The young Taikang became the ruler of the Xia dynasty.

00:00:09.628 --> 00:00:14.788
But Taikang loved hunting and disliked attending to state affairs.

00:00:15.138 --> 00:00:18.954
He often rode out with his attendants to chase game in the wilds.

00:00:19.304 --> 00:00:25.256
Away from the capital for long stretches, Taikang left the court with no one in charge.

00:00:25.606 --> 00:00:30.478
The people gradually grew resentful, and the kingdom slid into disorder.

00:00:30.828 --> 00:00:35.388
At this moment, Hou Yi, chief of the Youqiong clan, seized his chance.

00:00:35.738 --> 00:00:39.986
Hou Yi was a master archer, with a powerful army under his command.

00:00:40.336 --> 00:00:43.888
Returning from the hunt, Taikang tried to go back to his capital.

00:00:44.238 --> 00:00:48.102
But Hou Yi sent troops to block him and would not let him enter the city.

00:00:48.452 --> 00:00:52.172
And so Taikang lost his throne and his power.

00:00:52.522 --> 00:00:57.298
This story reminds rulers to take their responsibilities seriously.

